<!-- PART I -->
<div class="section-divider"><div class="part-title">Part I</div><div class="part-subtitle">Business Plan</div></div>

<!-- 1 -->
<h1>1. Executive Summary</h1>
<p>Chartvolt is a <strong>gamified trading infrastructure platform</strong> designed to increase engagement, retention, and monetization in retail trading.</p>
<p>The platform combines:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Professional-grade trading tools with real-time charting and 106 technical indicators</li>
  <li>Structured competition mechanics with monetized weekly tournaments</li>
  <li>Peer-to-peer challenges with platform rake</li>
  <li>A <strong>Game Master ecosystem</strong> where power-users pay monthly subscriptions to create competitions and earn referral income</li>
  <li>Badge and milestone progression systems (266+ badges, 169+ milestones)</li>
  <li>Multi-tenant white-label deployment for brokers and prop firms</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Revenue is generated through three engines:</strong></p>
<p><strong>B2B &mdash; White-Label Licensing:</strong> Recurring SaaS revenue from brokers and prop firms. &euro;6,000/month + &euro;10,000 setup fee per client.</p>
<p><strong>B2C &mdash; Engagement Monetization:</strong> Competition rake (30%), challenge rake (30%), premium subscriptions, and marketplace commissions.</p>
<p><strong>Game Master Network:</strong> Monthly subscriptions (&euro;100&ndash;&euro;1,000/month) sold to community leaders who create competitions and recruit new traders via referral codes, driving zero-CAC user acquisition.</p>

<div class="callout">The business is profitable from Year 1 with a lean 6-person team and efficient &euro;8K/month marketing. Year 1 delivers &euro;122,000 profit, Year 2 delivers &euro;562,000, and Year 3 delivers &euro;1,340,000. Cumulative 3-year profit: &euro;2,024,000.</div>

<table>
  <tr><th>Metric</th><th>Year 1</th><th>Year 2</th><th>Year 3</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Total Users (organic + GM-referred)</td><td>500</td><td>1,000</td><td>2,000</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Game Masters</td><td>25</td><td>60</td><td>120</td></tr>
  <tr><td>White-Label Clients</td><td>2</td><td>5</td><td>8</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Total Revenue</td><td>&euro;560,000</td><td>&euro;1,135,000</td><td>&euro;2,040,000</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Total Costs</td><td>&euro;438,000</td><td>&euro;573,000</td><td>&euro;700,000</td></tr>
  <tr class="total-row"><td>Net Profit</td><td class="positive">&euro;122,000</td><td class="positive">&euro;562,000</td><td class="positive">&euro;1,340,000</td></tr>
  <tr><td>EBITDA</td><td>&euro;125,000</td><td>&euro;567,000</td><td>&euro;1,348,000</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Net Margin</td><td>21.8%</td><td>49.5%</td><td>65.7%</td></tr>
</table>

<p><strong>Current Status:</strong> MVP complete. Full platform operational.</p>
<p><strong>Funding Sought:</strong> &euro;300,000 seed investment for marketing, working capital, infrastructure scaling, and sales development.</p>

<!-- 2 -->
<h1>2. Market Opportunity</h1>
<p>Retail trading participation continues to grow globally. The global online trading platform market is projected to exceed USD 15 billion by 2028. However:</p>
<p><strong>Trader retention is low.</strong> 70% of new traders churn within 90 days.</p>
<p><strong>Platform differentiation is limited.</strong> Most platforms offer identical tools.</p>
<p><strong>Brokers compete on acquisition costs.</strong> CAC ranges &euro;200&ndash;800 per trader.</p>
<p><strong>Community engagement is underdeveloped.</strong> Social and competitive features are absent or superficial.</p>
<p><strong>Chartvolt addresses all four problems</strong> by embedding gamification, competitions, progression, and a Game Master community network into trading:</p>
<ul>
  <li>2&ndash;3x longer session duration through achievements</li>
  <li>Monetizable engagement through competitions and challenges</li>
  <li>Turnkey WL retention solution for brokers</li>
  <li>Switching costs through progress, badges, and leaderboard position</li>
  <li><strong>Game Masters as paid micro-influencers</strong> self-funding user acquisition</li>
</ul>

<!-- 3 -->
<h1>3. Product Overview</h1>
<h2>Trading Infrastructure</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Real-time WebSocket price streaming (Massive.com)</li>
  <li>66 built-in + 40 premium marketplace indicators</li>
  <li>Strategy signal overlays, candlestick charting, multi-timeframe (1m&ndash;1W)</li>
</ul>

<h2>Gamification Engine</h2>
<ul>
  <li>169+ milestones across themed worlds, 266+ badges, level progression</li>
  <li>Weekly competitions with prize pools, P2P challenges, global leaderboards</li>
</ul>

<h2>Game Master Ecosystem</h2>
<p>GMs purchase monthly packages to create competitions, earn referral commissions, and build trading communities.</p>
<h3>Game Master Tiers</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Starter (&euro;100/mo)</th><th>Pro (&euro;300/mo)</th><th>Elite (&euro;500/mo)</th><th>Legend (&euro;1,000/mo)</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Competitions per day</td><td>1</td><td>3</td><td>5</td><td>10</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Max participants</td><td>30</td><td>75</td><td>100</td><td>150</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Referral on competition entries</td><td>2%</td><td>4%</td><td>6%</td><td>15%</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Referral on challenge entries</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>6%</td><td>15%</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Referral code &amp; dashboard</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Advanced</td><td>Advanced + Custom</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Featured listing</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>How the Game Master Flywheel Works</h3>
<p>1. GM buys a package (&euro;100&ndash;&euro;1,000/month).<br>
2. Gets unique referral link. Promotes to audience.<br>
3. Referred users enter competitions/challenges. Platform takes 30% fee.<br>
4. GM earns 2&ndash;15% from the platform&rsquo;s 30% cut.<br>
5. GM recruits more users to maximize earnings.<br>
6. More users = more competitions = more subscriptions = more revenue.</p>

<div class="callout"><strong>Key:</strong> Every GM is a self-funded acquisition channel. Platform pays &euro;0 CAC for GM-referred users. Referral payouts come from the platform fee, not additional cost.</div>

<h3>GM ROI Examples</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Tier</th><th>Cost</th><th>Break-Even</th><th>Example</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Starter</td><td>&euro;100/mo</td><td>10 users &times; 1 comp</td><td>10 &times; &euro;500 &times; 2% = &euro;100</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Pro</td><td>&euro;300/mo</td><td>15 users &times; 1 comp</td><td>15 &times; &euro;500 &times; 4% = &euro;300</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Elite</td><td>&euro;500/mo</td><td>12 users &times; 1 comp + 2 challenges</td><td>12 &times; (&euro;30 + &euro;6) = &euro;432+</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Legend</td><td>&euro;1,000/mo</td><td>14 users &times; 1 comp</td><td>14 &times; &euro;500 &times; 15% = &euro;1,050</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Marketplace Ecosystem</h2>
<ul><li>Premium indicators, strategies, avatars, GM packages, AI content, 30% commission</li></ul>

<h2>White-Label Capability</h2>
<ul><li>Multi-tenant, custom branding, separate DB, full feature parity, &lt;24h deployment</li></ul>

<h2>Technology Stack</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Layer</th><th>Technology</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Frontend</td><td>Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Backend</td><td>Node.js, MongoDB/Mongoose, WebSocket (Socket.io)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Infrastructure</td><td>Hostinger VPS, PM2, Upstash Redis</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Payments</td><td>Stripe, Nuvei</td></tr>
  <tr><td>KYC / AI / Data</td><td>Veriff, OpenAI GPT-4o, Massive.com</td></tr>
</table>

